  "findings": [
    "Chip padding now matches the Vanilla compact contract: Foundry uses 8px/8px side insets around 14/20px value text, which is in line with the panel-preset target.",
    "Chip lead/value typography now routes through the dedicated compact UI roles: the lead uses real small-caps with 0.7px tracking and the value sits on the 14/20px small-text line, matching the Vanilla split contract.",
    "Standalone badge geometry is effectively converged: Foundry's shortest badge is 15.20x16px versus Vanilla's 16x16px, leaving only a small residual aspect delta of -0.80px.",
    "Nested badge spacing is aligned with the chip contract: Foundry matches Vanilla's 8px badge gap and stays within 0.61px on the trailing inset.",
    "Status labels now match the Vanilla x-small contract: Foundry uses 12/16px text with no uppercase transform and 8/8px inline padding."
